- Only classify an issue as requiring a build environment (categories 2 or 3) when it's ABSOLUTELY NECESSARY to actually build and run the code to verify if the solution works.

GitHub Issue:
Post Date: 2018-12-19T15:27:01Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: local variable messes up async result (goto loop vs. scope of captured variable)
Description: **Version Used**: 
Visual Studio Professional 2017 15.9.4

**Steps to Reproduce**:
- Console Application
- .NET Framework 4.7.1
- Any CPU  

Compile and run following code:

```
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

class Program
{
	static void Main()
	{
		Task.Run(async () =>
		{
			Begin:
			var result = await FooAsync();
			Task.Run(async () =>
			{
				await Task.Yield();
				Console.WriteLine(result);
			});
			if (result < 9) goto Begin;
		}).Wait();
		Console.ReadKey();
	}

	static int i = 0;
	static object o = new object();

	static async Task<int> FooAsync()
	{
		await Task.Yield();
		lock (o)
			return i++;
	}
}
```

**Expected Behavior**:
Numbers 0...9 are displayed once.

**Actual Behavior**:
Some numbers are missing and some numbers are displayed more than once.


